This allow the usage of URL objects in the Link component, `Router#push` and `Router#replace`. See #1341. It use [Node.js url module](https://nodejs.org/api/url.html#url_url_format_urlobject) so you can use every [URL objects property](https://nodejs.org/api/url.html#url_url_strings_and_url_objects).

I think this is really useful, especially if you have urls with many query params or dynamic ones from props and states.

*Example usage*:
```js
// pages/index.js with Link
import Link from 'next/link'

export default () => (
  <Link href={{ pathname: '/about', query: { name: 'Zeit' }}}>
    <a>Go to <code>/about?name=Zeit</code></a>
  </Link>
)
```

```js
// pages/about.js with Router
import Router from 'next/router'

const handleClick = () => Router.push({ pathname: '/' })

export default (props) => (
  <div>
    <h1>Hello {props.url.query.name}</h1>
    <button onClick={handleClick}>Go home</button>
  </div>
)
```

![demo](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/3165635/26286839/b13e5534-3e6e-11e7-9f91-61df21dd236c.gif)

